<title>JAPAN: Japan welcomes Clinton re-election.</title>
<headline>Japan welcomes Clinton re-election.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan welcomed Bill Clinton's re-election as U.S. president on Wednesday, saying it ensured the continuation of stable relations with its main ally.</p>
<p>Top government spokesman Seiroku Kajiyama told reporters Japan expected even closer and friendlier relations with the new Clinton administration.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect that our close and friendly relations will be reinforced. Unless we both make an effort to do so, it will not be good for us or the world,&quot; Kajiyama said.</p>
</text>
